date: 2026-07-29T23:41:12-04:00
---

Herald is mundane and godly at the same time. They are the most average of all, an amalgam of everyone you’ve ever seen, and yet they exude a dignity that almost compels one to worship them. If, however, one pierces past the glamer the Herald insists upon, they will see the strange anatomy lying beneath. A chin, cleft completely in twain, forms jagged mandibles. Small dotted secondary eyes orbit the two humanoid ones. Antennae sprout from the forehead. A circular horn-like protrusion sprouts from the chest.

A likeness of Herald, a horned humanoid atop a mountain of corpses, stands on one of the six god doors in the fane beneath the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/Gas-n-Go|Gas-n-Go]]. Behind the door is an armory.

The saboteur in [[Geography/Istria/Iomenei/index|Iomenei]], the elven fluid master [[People/Gerhard|Gerhard]], had a jaw split into mandibles and small closed eyelids dotted around his eyes, and had scratched the mark of a horn inside a circle into the bedpost where he slept. [[People/Barlow Crane|Barlow Crane]], reading the emotions left on a sabotaged lubricant line, saw that face and sensed only religious devotion.
